# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Node (installer/tooling, if any)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tgz

# Local scratch / test projects
/tmp/
scratch/
*.local

# Working handoffs / design deep-dives (local only, not published)
/RESUME.md
/design-notes/

# Raw planning queue — local recall only, keeps candid working notes out of the public repo
/.planning/CAPTURE.md

# Joined run record — local diagnostics only, one machine's routing/provider/worker events
/.planning/trace.jsonl

# Triage working copies — these hold copies of the raw planning queue, the same
# candid text the /.planning/CAPTURE.md line above withholds, so tracking them
# would republish exactly what that line exists to keep out of the public repo.
# Matched on the directory name at any depth under /.planning/, NOT on one fixed
# parent: a milestone close MOVES phases/<N>/ to _archive-<label>/<N>/ and
# commits everything under it, so a pattern anchored to phases/ would stop
# ignoring these copies at exactly the moment they get staged. The same reason
# covers tasks/<name>/ and spikes/<name>/, which are tracked trees too.
/.planning/**/triage-work/
